Good call � web is much simpler to run and debug. Here's the updated guide:

---

## Revised Stack

| Layer | Choice | Reason |
|---|---|---|
| Framework | React + TypeScript (Vite) | Fast, lightweight, no mobile complexity |
| Storage | IndexedDB via `idb` library | Browser-native persistent storage, no backend |
| Notifications | Web Notifications API (native browser) | Built-in, no extra library |
| Routing | React Router v6 | Simple page navigation |
| UI | shadcn/ui + Tailwind CSS | Clean, modern, easy to customise |
| Date handling | `date-fns` | Same as before |

---

## What Changes From Mobile Version

| Aspect | Mobile (Expo) | Web (Vite) |
|---|---|---|
| Run command | `expo start` | `npm run dev` ? opens `localhost:5173` |
| Storage | SQLite on device | IndexedDB in browser |
| Notifications | Native push | Browser notification popups |
| Installation | Expo Go app needed | Just a browser tab |
| Deployment | App store | Vercel / Netlify (one command) |

